Description: graphical control surface for a whisper.cpp transcription server
 Shoki is a GTK4/libadwaita desktop application that sends audio and video
 files to a whisper.cpp server and saves the transcripts it returns. It puts
 the server's request parameters -- output format, translation, initial
 prompt, subtitle tuning -- behind a single window instead of a command line.
 .
 A standalone helper, shoki-transcribe, is installed alongside it, together
 with a KDE service menu so that files can be transcribed by right-click from
 Dolphin. The helper never launches the application and reads its settings at
 runtime, so the two share one configuration and cannot drift apart.
 .
 Shoki does not include a transcription engine. It requires a reachable
 whisper.cpp server, which it treats as an external HTTP service.
